      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-95310",
      ":question/problem": "A coin is flipped $6$ times. Let $X$ represent the number of times the coin lands on heads. Under the null hypothesis that the coin is fair, what is the critical region of a two-tailed test at a significance level of $5%$?\n\n*Hint: You may use the table below, representing the probability distribution of $X$ under the null hypothesis.*\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X = x)$ | $0.0156$ | $0.0938$ | $0.2344$ | $0.3125$ | $0.2344$ | $0.0938$ | $0.0156$ |\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
